QUESTION_PROMPT_BEGIN bytes=370
Find KE of product particles in,
Pi(+) = mu(+) + nu
here Pi(+) is stationary.
Rest mass of Pi(+) & mu(+) is 139.6 MeV & 105.7 MeV respectively.

Choices:
A. 7.2 MeV, 32.8 MeV
B. 4.12 MeV, 29.8 MeV
C. 2.84 MeV, 26.8 MeV
D. 3.52 MeV, 20.8 MeV

Solve the question. At the end, write exactly one final line in this format and do not write anything after it:
Answer: <letter>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=812
We have the decay:
π⁺ → μ⁺ + ν_μ  
π⁺ at rest.  
Given: m_π = 139.6 MeV/c², m_μ = 105.7 MeV/c², neutrino mass ≈ 0.

Energy conservation:  
m_π c² = E_μ + E_ν  
Momentum conservation:  
|p_μ| = |p_ν| = p.

For muon: E_μ = √(p²c² + m_μ²c⁴)  
For neutrino: E_ν = p c.

So:  
√(p²c² + m_μ²c⁴) + p c = m_π c².

Let x = p c. Then:  
√(x² + m_μ²) + x = m_π.

Solve:  
√(x² + m_μ²) = m_π - x  
Square:  
x² + m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π x + x²  
⇒ m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π x  
⇒ 2 m_π x = m_π² - m_μ²  
⇒ x = (m_π² - m_μ²) / (2 m_π).

Numerically:  
m_π² = (139.6)² = 19488.16  
m_μ² = (105.7)² = 11172.49  
Difference = 8315.67  
Divide by 2 m_π = 279.2 → x = 8315.67 / 279.2 ≈ 29.78 MeV.

So neutrino KE = E_ν = x ≈ 29.8 MeV.  
Muon
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

